  "engineering_rules": [
    "Prefer small coherent modules with explicit interfaces and ownership.",
    "Prefer reusable helpers and reusable workflows over copy-paste families.",
    "Tests must assert behavior or evidence, not incidental wording or implementation text.",
    "A test is not a gate until CI demonstrably executes it.",
    "Production schema and function behavior must remain reconstructable from source control.",
    "No hidden magic score, threshold, authority or deployment rule may remain undocumented.",
    "No new brain, registry, queue, calendar, analytics store or learning store when an existing canonical capability can be extended.",
    "Use current task-relevant external evidence when technology currency can materially change the answer or implementation.",
    "Adopt frontier technology only through a reversible, measurable experiment with rollback or fallback.",
    "Measure engineering speed and instability with explicit evidence completeness; unknown values are never synthetic zero.",
    "Flaky-test diagnostics never override a required failure and rerun-until-green is prohibited.",
    "Recovery is proven only by fresh successful bounded rehearsal evidence, not documentation alone.",
    "Meta-learning recommendations can only change Engineering OS through the normal protected delivery path.",
